<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends easier on dollar demand.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends easier on dollar demand.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka closed easier at 42.5460/42.5500 to dollar in interbank trading compared with the previous 42.5430/42.5480, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the taka, after opening unchanged, slipped on demand for dollars from importers.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates ended unchanged at 4.00 to 4.75 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
